From 48b395191aea45dc8af584138f55578a550e816b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Procee <sn125164@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:37:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] backend/drm: skip legacy gamma on CRTCs without it

drm_atomic_connector_prepare() picked the legacy gamma ioctl whenever the
CRTC has no GAMMA_LUT property. Atomic-only drivers without any gamma
support (e.g. apple-dcp on Apple Silicon: no GAMMA_LUT, no
GAMMA_LUT_SIZE, legacy gamma_size 0) were thus routed into
drm_legacy_crtc_set_gamma(), which fails, and that cancels the whole
atomic commit.

wlr_scene resets the gamma LUT (NULL color transform) on every output
enable, so on such drivers the first commit after "output power on"
always failed and the display stayed off. The test commit doesn't
catch it: wlr_output_test_state() drops the unchanged NULL color
transform via output_compare_state(), while wlr_backend_commit() keeps
it.

Only fall back to the legacy interface when the CRTC has a legacy gamma
size. Without any gamma support, treat a reset as a no-op and reject a
real LUT, so gamma-control clients still get a failed test.

Based on the analysis and patch by Thomas Glanzmann in #4123.
---
 backend/drm/atomic.c | 19 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/backend/drm/atomic.c b/backend/drm/atomic.c
index a7ea3a7e7..94f8a4a40 100644
--- a/backend/drm/atomic.c
+++ b/backend/drm/atomic.c
@@ -349,18 +349,23 @@ bool drm_atomic_connector_prepare(struct wlr_drm_connector_state *state, bool mo
 			lut = tr->lut_3x1d;
 		}
 
-		// Fallback to legacy gamma interface when gamma properties are not
-		// available (can happen on older Intel GPUs that support gamma but not
-		// degamma).
-		if (crtc->props.gamma_lut == 0) {
-			if (!drm_legacy_crtc_set_gamma(drm, crtc, dim, lut)) {
+		if (crtc->props.gamma_lut != 0) {
+			if (!create_gamma_lut_blob(drm, dim, lut, &gamma_lut)) {
 				return false;
 			}
-		} else {
-			if (!create_gamma_lut_blob(drm, dim, lut, &gamma_lut)) {
+		} else if (crtc->legacy_gamma_size != 0) {
+			// Fallback to legacy gamma interface when gamma properties are not
+			// available (can happen on older Intel GPUs that support gamma but not
+			// degamma).
+			if (!drm_legacy_crtc_set_gamma(drm, crtc, dim, lut)) {
 				return false;
 			}
+		} else if (lut != NULL) {
+			wlr_drm_conn_log(conn, WLR_DEBUG,
+				"Color transform not supported: CRTC has no gamma LUT");
+			return false;
 		}
+		// Resetting the gamma LUT of a CRTC without one is a no-op
 	}
 
 	uint32_t fb_damage_clips = 0;
-- 
